From 05ba9149f1f1c063c83123ba675ec4ead1550819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:36:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): spend budget reopens on a human answer; per-card
 override for standing cards [daveey]

Follow-up to #3033 (review t_01a1daf04c8ed96b, card t_01a1daf392bf6005).

Defect 1: a card that used up its 15 runs while blocked on needs_input went
straight to triage the tick after David answered it (comment + unblock), with
no run, so he had to promote it too. The budget window now also opens at the
newest human answer: a `commented` event with writer_kind='human' or a chat's
verified `relayed_human` relay -- the no-progress budget's rule. Agent comments,
legacy kind-less notes and a bare `unblocked` (no actor) still do not reopen it.

Defect 2: standing cards meant to run indefinitely (t_7d17e13d Upkeep shepherd,
217 counted runs) were triaged every 15 runs. A card can now carry its own
limits: `kanban_spend_budget.set_override` / `hermes kanban spend-budget <id>
[--runs N] [--cache-read-tokens N] [--exempt] [--clear] --reason ...` writes a
`spend_budget_set` event (who, why, limits; newest wins; 0 = no limit; an unset
field keeps the board's) plus a card comment. hold() applies it, re-reads it
under the write lock, and marks `override: true` on a triage it causes. Never
inferred from a title; worker and delegate_task shells are fenced from the verb.

RED (before the fix): 15 new tests failed in
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_spend_budget.py, including
test_a_human_answer_opens_a_new_window[human|relayed] reproducing
no_progress_held == [(tid, 'spend_budget:triage')] with 0 spawns.
GREEN: 36/36 pass. Docs: website/docs/user-guide/features/kanban.md
"Spend budget".
